    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Chronological sequence of Dynasties: Mamluk (1206–1290), Khilji (1290–1320), Tughlaq (1320–1414), Sayyid (1414–1451), and Lodi (1451–1526).",
        "Key Terminology: Iqta (land assignment), Tanka (silver coin), Jital (copper coin), Dagh (branding of horses), and Chehra (soldier identity roll).",
        "Alauddin Khilji was the first ruler of the Delhi Sultanate to maintain a standing army paid directly in cash.",
        "The First Battle of Panipat (1526 AD) saw Babur defeat Ibrahim Lodi, bringing an end to the Delhi Sultanate."
      ],
      "id": "ligebj2"
    },
